  "name": "Example: Raising a Fraction to the Power of Negative One",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)^{-1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The expression $\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)^{-1}$ means the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{2}{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{3}{2}.\n$$",
